<h2 id="chapter1">Chapter 1: Lab Partners</h2>
<p><b>Ivy Alvarez</b><br>
Beautiful valedictorian. Rich family, big house, but it’s always quiet.<br>
Busy parents who are never home. Raised by maids, not hugs.<br>
Top of the class because it’s the one thing she can control.<br>
And she flinches at loud sounds — the belt snapping, a car horn. Still gets to her.</p>

<p><b>Jace Miller</b><br>
Basketball captain. Loud family, always people over, mom yelling "dinner!" from the kitchen.<br>
The opposite of Ivy’s world. He’s chaos, but he’s warm.</p>

<p>No wonder they clash. She thinks he’s reckless. He thinks she’s ice.</p>

<p><i>opening scene:</i></p>

<p>Ms. Carter: "Ivy Alvarez and Jace Miller. Lab partners."</p>
<p>The class snickered. Ivy didn’t look up. Her knuckles were white around her pen.</p>
<p>Jace leaned back in his chair. "Damn. The robot and the class clown. This’ll be fun."</p>
<p>Ivy finally met his eyes. "I’m not a robot. And if you break one beaker, I’m telling Ms. Carter it was you."</p>
<p>He smirked. "If you scream when the Bunsen burner pops, I’m telling everyone."</p>
<p>She didn’t. But her shoulders did that tiny jerk she hated.</p>

<h2 id="chapter2">Chapter 2: Detention</h2>
<p><i>New scene - Lab, week 2:</i><br>
Lab assignment.</p>

<p>Jace slid into the seat next to her, smelling like cologne and yesterday.<br>
"Hey Ice Queen. You bring the worksheet?"</p>

<p>Ivy didn’t answer. She was measuring liquid, hands steady.</p>

<p>"Yo, are you mad I didn’t text Maya back? She’s clingy." He laughed. "Girls are wild."</p>

<p>The Bunsen burner clicked on. Ivy’s hand jerked. A drop splashed.<br>
Jace caught her wrist before she could burn herself. "Whoa. You good?"</p>

<p>She yanked away, causing the beaker to crash into pieces.<br>
"Don’t touch me."</p>

<p>His grin faded a little. "Chill. I was just helping."</p>

<p>"Right," she said quietly. "That’s what you do."</p>

<p>Silence. The only sound was the burner.</p>

<p>"Jace, Ivy detention you both 😡" Miss Carter yelled.</p>

<p>"Looks like Miss Perfect is getting a detention today" he snickered.</p>

